{
  "_": [
    "Issue #54: the red 'new messages' line, and the rail mark that jumps to it.",
    "",
    "This is the one thing about the line that a widget test cannot answer. The",
    "index math is guarded in test/widget/unread_divider_test.dart and the",
    "capture rules in unread_marker_test.dart, but both of those hand the",
    "pointer in by hand. What is unproven until two real apps do it is that the",
    "pointer is captured at the right MOMENT: the sidebar marks a DM seen from",
    "its selection callback before the pane exists, the pane marks it seen",
    "again on load, and the scroll handler marks it seen a third time on",
    "arrival at the bottom. Any one of those clobbering the entry pointer",
    "erases the line the instant it is drawn, and every one of them is real",
    "only when a message actually arrives over the relay.",
    "",
    "The journey: a and b become friends, a reads the conversation, a walks",
    "away, b sends two messages, a comes back. The line belongs above b's",
    "FIRST message and nowhere else.",
    "",
    "run: powershell -File scripts/fleet.ps1 -Scenario unread_line"
  ],
  "peers": [
    "a",
    "b"
  ],
  "steps": [
